  "sourceSemantics": [
    "The installed basilica floor comes from the 483 x 479 native embedded plan on Churches of Rome page 15, xref 99. It avoids the PDF page's non-uniform image placement.",
    "The installed grottoes floor comes from the distinct 880 x 784 native embedded plan on page 63, xref 261, cropped to the documented plan area at y=740.",
    "Black basilica numerals and text, red grotto labels, compass, decorative background, and generated bridges are excluded. Emitted wall pixels are always a subset of source ink.",
    "Eight selectable spaces come from source-wall components. Closing kernels are selectors only; each per-space overlay and checkpoint reports no source-wall crossing and no selector pixels emitted as walls.",
    "The 1966 Accademia delle Scienze di Torino Fondo Millon slide 48_13_060 is rectified from the photographed paper corners. Its dome-circle axis ratio is 1.0064907, but the drawing is historical and partial, so it is support evidence only and is not a model floor."
  ],
